@d_investigate
view-if: chan_can_decree and chp_bureau_state = "held" and war_shadows_seen
subtitle: −2 political capital. +1 evidence, and the search for the Sith Lord advances. Takes the turn.
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {! SW.decree(Q, 'investigate'); !}

The loyal analysts of the Bureau of Intelligence are set loose on the questions the Caucus has been asking for years. Their reports come straight to our Chancellor's desk.

@giveback
view-if: rc_chancellor and chan_powers > 0
subtitle: Hand one of the office's powers back to the Senate for good. Faith +3; the precedent falls by 1. Takes the turn.

= Return a Power

Which power will our Chancellor give back? Each is handed back for good: what checks it takes effect as if the Senate had passed it.

- @gb_gavel
- @gb_guard
- @gb_staff
- @gb_decrees
- @gb_army
- @gb_bureau
- @gb_holonet
- @gb_term
- @gb_jedi
- @gb_banks
- @gb_security
- @gb_governors
- @go_back_page

@gb_gavel
title: The gavel.
subtitle: As if the Senate had passed an independent Speaker.
view-if: chp_gavel_state = "held"
on-arrival: {! SW.returnPower(Q, 'gavel'); !}

Our Chancellor returns [+ returned_name +] to the Senate. The Caucus's own senators are the most surprised: power is not usually given back. Faith in the Republic rises a little.

@gb_guard
title: The Senate Guard.
subtitle: As if the Senate had passed the Guard returned to the Senate.
view-if: chp_guard_state = "held"
on-arrival: {! SW.returnPower(Q, 'guard'); !}

Our Chancellor returns [+ returned_name +] to the Senate. The Caucus's own senators are the most surprised: power is not usually given back. Faith in the Republic rises a little.

